        <span style="background:rgba(31,111,235,0.15); color:var(--gh-accent-fg); border:1px solid rgba(31,111,235,0.4); font-size:.78rem; font-weight:700; padding:.2rem .6rem; border-radius:12px;">Open Source</span>
    </div>
    
    <p>
        <strong>GitPHP</strong> is completely open-source and engineered to be lightweight, high-performance, and trivial to install on any shared Linux hosting or dedicated VPS without requiring Docker or bloated runtime services.
    </p>

    <h3>📋 System Requirements:</h3>
    <ul style="padding-left:1.4rem; line-height:1.8;">
        <li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Modern Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+, Debian 11+, AlmaLinux 9+, Rocky Linux, RHEL).</li>
        <li><strong>PHP Version:</strong> PHP 8.1 or newer (PHP 8.2 / 8.3 recommended) with extensions: <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">pdo_mysql</code>, <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">mbstring</code>, <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">curl</code>, <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">intl</code>, <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">sodium</code>, <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">fileinfo</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Database:</strong> MariaDB 10.6+ or MySQL 8.0+.</li>
        <li><strong>Git Engine:</strong> Git 2.30+ installed server-wide and available in <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">$PATH</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Package Manager:</strong> Composer 2.x.</li>
        <li><strong>Web Server:</strong> OpenLiteSpeed / LiteSpeed, Nginx, or Apache.</li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="border:0; border-top:1px solid var(--gh-border-default); margin:1.5rem 0;">

    <h3>🚀 Quick Command-Line (CLI) Installation:</h3>

    <h4>1. Clone Repository &amp; Install Dependencies:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># Clone repository into web directory
git clone https://github.com/ysnapp/gitphp.git /var/www/gitphp
cd /var/www/gitphp

# Install production dependencies
composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader</code></pre>

    <h4>2. Configure Environment &amp; Database:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># Copy configuration template
cp config/config.example.php config/config.php

# Edit database credentials and application settings
nano config/config.php</code></pre>

    <h4>3. Run the Automated Installer:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># Execute the interactive CLI installer
php bin/install.php

# Or run the browser installer wizard by navigating to:
# https://your-domain.com/install.php</code></pre>

    <h4>4. Set Permissions &amp; Run Diagnostic:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># Grant ownership to your web user (www-data / nobody / site user)
chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/gitphp/
chmod -R 755 /var/www/gitphp/
chmod -R 775 /var/www/gitphp/data/ /var/www/gitphp/storage/

# Run the health & push verification script
php bin/fix-push.php</code></pre>

    <div class="gh-docs-callout ok">✅ After completing setup, remove <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">public_html/install.php</code> or the application will automatically block access for security.</div>
</section>
