{# ── 3. Dedicated Card: Token Push (PAT) ⭐️ ── #}
{% if current_cat == 'all' or 'token-push' in allowed %}
<section id="token-push" class="gh-docs-section" style="border: 2px solid rgba(56,139,253,0.4); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(56,139,253,0.03) 0%, transparent 100%); border-radius:10px; padding:1.75rem;">
    <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem;">
        <h2 style="margin:0;"><span class="gh-docs-num" style="background:#238636; color:#fff;">⭐️</span> Personal Access Token Push (PAT)</h2>
        <span style="background:rgba(56,139,253,0.15); color:var(--gh-accent-fg); border:1px solid rgba(56,139,253,0.4); font-size:.78rem; font-weight:700; padding:.2rem .6rem; border-radius:12px;">Recommended for Security & CI/CD</span>
    </div>
    
    <p>
        <strong>Personal Access Tokens (PAT)</strong> let you authenticate and push to your repositories securely without exposing or entering your primary account password.
        Tokens are generated as <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">gtp_…</code> strings and stored safely hashed (SHA-256) in the database.
    </p>

    <div class="gh-docs-grid" style="margin:1.25rem 0;">
        <div class="gh-docs-card">
            <h4>1. Generate Token</h4>
            <p>Under <strong>Settings → Access Tokens</strong> (or direct URL <code>/settings/tokens</code>), choose a name, select <code>write</code> scope, and copy your token.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gh-docs-card">
            <h4>2. Use with Git</h4>
            <p>Paste the token in place of your password whenever running <code>git push</code> or <code>git clone</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gh-docs-card">
            <h4>3. Instant Revocation</h4>
            <p>If a token is leaked or no longer needed, revoke it in one click without altering your account credentials.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Practical Usage Examples:</h3>
    
    <h4>1. Cache locally via Git Credential Store:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># Enable local credential caching
git config --global credential.helper store

# Push and input credentials once
git push https://{{ app_url|replace({'https://':'', 'http://':''}) }}/{{ owner }}/my-project.git main
# Username: {{ owner }}
# Password: gtp_your_token_here</code></pre>

    <h4>2. Direct Remote URL with Token:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code>git remote set-url origin https://{{ owner }}:gtp_your_token_here@{{ app_url|replace({'https://':'', 'http://':''}) }}/{{ owner }}/my-project.git
git push origin main</code></pre>

    <h4>3. Continuous Integration (CI/CD) — GitHub Actions & GitLab CI:</h4>
<pre class="gh-docs-code" dir="ltr"><code># In GitHub Actions:
- name: Push to GitPHP
  env:
    GIT_TOKEN: ${{ '{{' }} secrets.GITPHP_TOKEN {{ '}}' }}
  run: |
    git remote set-url origin https://{{ owner }}:${GIT_TOKEN}@{{ app_url|replace({'https://':'', 'http://':''}) }}/{{ owner }}/my-project.git
    git push origin main</code></pre>

    <div class="gh-docs-callout ok">💡 <strong>Token Scopes:</strong> The <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">write</code> scope allows pushing, cloning, and full API access, while the <code class="gh-docs-inline-code">read</code> scope is restricted to cloning and reading API data only.</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

